# Agent Model Policy

## QA pipeline chain (Sonnet 5 — pinned)

These agents use **`model: claude-sonnet-5-thinking-high`** so subagent cards match
Sonnet 5 intent even when Cursor `inherit` is unreliable:

| Agent | Model |
|-------|--------|
| `qa-automation-pipeline` | `claude-sonnet-5-thinking-high` |
| `playwright-test-generator` | `claude-sonnet-5-thinking-high` |
| `playwright-test-healer` | `claude-sonnet-5-thinking-high` |
| `playwright-test-generator` / `playwright-test-healer` | `claude-sonnet-5-thinking-high` |

**Quota:** draws from **Other Models** pool. Platform may still fall back to Composer
when included Sonnet usage is exhausted.

## Script-only agents (Composer — cheap pool)

| Agent | Model |
|-------|--------|
| `execute-raise-defects` | `composer-2.5-fast` |
| `defect-regression` | `composer-2.5-fast` |
| `fsd-figma-pipeline` | `composer-2.5-fast` |
| `fsd-excel-coverage-audit` | `composer-2.5-fast` |

## Task invocation rules

- Do **not** pass a conflicting explicit `model:` on Task for pipeline children.
- If subagent launch fails with usage limit, fall back to repo scripts in parent
  only when the user explicitly approves (see named-agent-invocation rule).
- Check Cursor **Usage / Spending** when limits hit mid-pipeline.
